          {
            "slice_type": "about",
            "variation": "default",
            "items": [],
            "primary": {
              "heading": "Our Mission is to Inspire Young & Fresh Perspectives to Reshape Indian Music",
              "subheading": "Svarit was founded in 2001 with the vision of promoting and propagating the rich tradition of Hindustani Raag Sangeet, as envisioned by the legendary vocalist Pandit Dinkar Kaikini.",
              "body": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Svarit, a Sanskrit word meaning “ascending towards the divine”, embodies our belief in music as a pathway to higher artistic and spiritual expression. Founded to preserve and promote the legacy of Indian Music as envisioned by Pandit Dinkar Kaikini, Svarit is rooted in a rich musical lineage that traces through the legacies of the great masters of Hindustani classical music, the likes of Pt. Vishnu Narayan Bhatkhande, Ustad Faiyaz Khan, Padma Bhushan Acharya S. N. Ratanjankar, Ustad Allarakha & Ustad Zakir Hussain.",
                  "spans": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Today, under the guidance of Pt. Yogesh Samsi and Smt. Aditi Kaikini Upadhya, Svarit is more than a trust. It is a vibrant cultural platform where tradition meets innovation. Through concerts, festivals, educational initiatives, artist development, and collaborative projects, we nurture excellence while ensuring our country's arts remain relevant, accessible, and inspiring for future generations. Svarit continues to celebrate heritage, foster creativity, and shape the future of Indian Music.",
                  "spans": []
                }
              ],
              "stats": "20+ Volunteers"
            }
          },
